# CONTEXT WHITELIST (ported from the private line, 2026-11-15) — SUPERSEDES the
# exclude-list approach. The legacy builder on a deploy host (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0)
# tar-streams the ENTIRE context to the daemon BEFORE the first RUN step. Residue in
# the checkout (DEV/, benchmarks/, scratch docs, venvs) otherwise rides to the daemon
# and can put the build in a long zero-step "Sending build context" stall.
# Whitelist EXACTLY what the Dockerfile COPYs; everything else stays on the host, out
# of the context. Image layers are IDENTICAL: this changes only what rides to the daemon.
*
!Dockerfile
!pyproject.toml
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!src
!migrations
!tools

# nested junk patterns REMAIN necessary on top of the whitelist: re-including a
# top-level dir (src, tools, ...) re-admits EVERYTHING under it, so fossil
# __pycache__/*.pyc inside keep-dirs rides unless explicitly re-excluded. Caught
# live 2026-10-16 on the private line: a stale src/api/__pycache__ pyc failed the
# Dockerfile non-root readability gate.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
